User: The diagonal of a particular square is 5 inches.  The diameter of a particular circle is also 5 inches.  By how many square inches is the area of the circle greater than the area of square?  Express your answer as a decimal to the nearest tenth. [asy]
draw((0,0)--(2,0)--(2,2)--(0,2)--cycle);
